PackageManager: Let a property allow updating an app signed with another key

Android only updates an app with an APK signed with the same key, so
testing a build of Kiosk Satellite signed with another key meant
uninstalling it first, which loses its data and its device owner status.

While persist.echo.pm.allow_resign is true, an app that is not a system
app may be updated with an APK signed with another key. It keeps its
data, its permissions, the permissions it declares and its device owner
status. System apps keep the usual check, and with the property unset
nothing changes.

